grain: unknown command frobnicate
grain 0.1.0 - a small, fast, embeddable language

usage:
  grain <file.gr> [args...]         run a program (same as grain run)
  grain run <file.gr> [args...]     run a program; `args` holds what follows it
  grain eval <source...>            run one line and print its value
  grain repl                        read and run lines until EOF or .quit
  grain serve <file.gr> [--port N] [--max-body 10m]  the program's ui.pane in a browser, not a window
  grain ps [--json]                 the grain programs, app hosts and ASQL engines running here
  grain open <url>                  a ui.pane program running on a server, in a native window (no HTML)
  grain check <file.gr>...          compile only and report every error
  grain dis <file.gr>               show the bytecode the compiler emitted
  grain build <file.gr> [-o out]    make one executable of the program (see grain build)
  grain test [file | dir]...        run the tests in *_test.gr files
  grain fmt [--check] <file | dir>  lay source out the one grain way
  grain lsp                         a language server for editors, on stdin/stdout
  grain host                        this machine's app host: runs, restarts and serves its apps
  grain app deploy|status|logs|...  apps, on this machine or another (`grain app help`)
  grain pkg init|add|list|vendor    package and dependency management (`grain pkg help`)
  grain debug <file.gr>             run in interactive step-by-step debugger
  grain version                     print the version

options (before the subcommand):
  --steps <n>                       stop a program after n instructions
  --no-jit                          interpret everything
  --safe                            native fn only on bytes: no ptr, extern fn, ffi or plugins
  --no-native                       refuse native fn altogether
